<title>USA: Marathon Oil cuts U.S. posted crude prices.</title>
<headline>Marathon Oil cuts U.S. posted crude prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents, effective Tuesday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.50 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $17.90 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $18.25 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.50.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
</text>
